          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I have stage 3 kidney disease and high blood pressure. Does the classification link the two, and what target does guidance describe for someone like me?",
          "answer": "Yes, there is a classification link between stage 3 kidney disease and high blood pressure. According to the coding document, \"the classification presumes a causal link between hypertension and chronic kidney disease and pairs them without being told to.\" This means when both conditions are documented, they are treated as related.\n\nFor your management and targets, recent guidance generally sets the blood pressure target below 130/80 mm Hg for optimal control (source: \"Coronary artery disease: secondary prevention after a diagnosis\"). Regular follow-up is recommended to monitor adherence, kidney function, and potassium levels, especially after beginning or adjusting treatment (source: \"Hypertension: diagnostic thresholds and blood-pressure targets\"). \n\nFor further dietary and lifestyle recommendations specific to managing hypertension, please consult with your clinician for tailored advice, as it involves adjustments that will best suit your individual health situation. \n\nI could not cover finer points of treatment options or specifics on medication adjustments you might discuss with your doctor.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
